  "verse_id": "ghat-p01-v9",
  "song": "ghat-p01",
  "verse": 9,
  "plain_english": "Drowned in sorrow-ocean's water; remembrance of your virtue alone keeps her afloat. The rivers' water melts the impurity. Why do you regard me, not wretched? Pained by deep cloud-rasa — when shall I abandon, friend, the burning of separation-born sorrow?",
